{
 "about": "Grass tip displacement per wind level. The bend is each build's own vertex-shader formula (src/desert.js vegMat, d172: shear d = wl*(lean..)*A*h^2; d173: rotation about the tuft root toward a shared 72-degree downwind lean, more the higher the point, chord-shortened as a curved stem), evaluated on the CPU on the live instance matrices, the scene's wind (st.wn), wind direction, gust clock and time, over 3 s (90 frames). Tips: the top 30 % (by height) of every blade of every grass/clump/dry tuft (sway 0.8) and reed (0.3) 2-12 m from the camera's tuft. downwindCm: horizontal tip shift along the wind; leanDeg: change of the tip's angle from the vertical about the tuft root, toward the wind; stretchPct: change of the tip's distance from the root (0 = no stretching). 'gust peak': the same at wind 1.0 counting only tip samples on tufts the gust field is on (>= 0.75, its clock set so the gust peaks at the camera's tuft).",
